### Goal Model Design

The goal model is structured to manage the food delivery and retrieval process efficiently in a hospital setting. It includes sub-goals for handling delivery requests, delivering food, determining retrieval capabilities, indicating correct meals, retrieving dirty dishes, and handling door openings. Each goal is decomposed into tasks that specify the actions required, considering the number of robots and locations involved.

### Goal and Task Tables

#### Goals

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|--------|------------|------|--------------------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| G1     | Manage Food Delivery and Retrieval Process | Ensure food delivery and retrieval processes are executed correctly. | - | Achieve | - | Ensures overall process success. |
| G2     | Handle Kitchen Delivery Requests | Process each kitchen delivery request. | - | Achieve | G1 | Processes each order. |
| G3     | Deliver Food to Inpatient Room | Deliver food to the specified room. | - | Perform | G2 | Executes the delivery action. |
| G4     | Determine Retrieval Capability | Check if the patient or companion can retrieve food. | - | Query | G3 | Gathers necessary information. |
| G5     | Indicate Correct Meal for Retrieval | Ensure the correct meal is retrieved. | - | Perform | G3 | Ensures correct meal is taken. |
| G6     | Retrieve Dirty Dishes from Room | Collect dirty dishes from the room. | - | Perform | G1 | Completes the full process. |
| G7     | Handle Dish Retrieval Process | Manage dish retrieval efficiently. | - | Achieve | G6 | Ensures dishes are retrieved. |
| G8     | Handle Door Opening Process | Ensure doors are opened correctly. | - | Achieve | G2, G6 | Facilitates access. |

#### Tasks

| Task ID | Task Title | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|------------|------|----------|----------|------------------|---------------|
| AT1     | Move to Kitchen | Navigate to the kitchen area. | AND | Kitchen | 1 | Single robot fetches order. |
| AT2     | Receive Order | Confirm order details. | AND | Kitchen | 1 | Sequential after moving. |
| AT3     | Move to Delivery Room | Navigate to the target room. | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Single robot delivers. |
| AT4     | Place Food on Table | Deposit food on the room table. | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Special skill required. |
| AT5     | Confirm Delivery | Verify food is delivered. | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Ensures success. |
| AT6     | Move to Tray Retrieval | Navigate to room for tray. | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Sequential steps follow. |
| AT7     | Park Near Tray | Position near the tray. | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Prepares for retrieval. |
| AT8     | Confirm Meal Retrieval | Ensure correct meal is taken. | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Prevents errors. |
| AT9     | Query Patient Record | Retrieve patient information. | Parallel | Hospital Database | 1 | Simultaneous checks. |
| AT10    | Check Companion Presence | Determine companion availability. | Parallel | Hospital Database | 1 | Parallel to patient info. |
| AT11    | Indicate Correct Meal | Signal correct meal. | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Clear communication. |
| AT12    | Move to Dish Pickup | Navigate to room for dishes. | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Single robot retrieval. |
| AT13    | Park Near Tray for Dishes | Position near tray for dishes. | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Prepares for retrieval. |
| AT14    | Retrieve Dishes | Collect dirty dishes. | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Completes task. |
| AT15    | Call Robot for Dishes | Signal robot to retrieve. | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Human initiation. |
| AT16    | Identify Caller | Determine who called. | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Verifies caller. |
| AT17    | Retrieve Dishes with Human | Collaborate with human. | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Combined effort. |
| AT18    | Two Robots Move to Room | Navigate with another robot. | Parallel | Patient Room | [2,2] | Simultaneous arrival. |
| AT19    | One Robot Parks | One robot waits. | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Supports the other. |
| AT20    | Retrieve Dishes Collaboratively | Two robots retrieve. | AND | Patient Room | 2 | Efficient teamwork. |
| AT21    | Move to Room for Door | Navigate for door access. | Parallel | Patient Room | [1,2] | Either one or two robots. |
| AT22    | Open Door with Human | Collaborate with human. | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Human assistance. |

### Logical Relationships

- **G2 -> AT1, AT2**: Sequential execution as the robot must first move to the kitchen before receiving the order.
- **G3 -> G31, G32**: OR decomposition since either placing food or tray retrieval can fulfill delivery.
- **G31 -> AT3, AT4, AT5**: Sequential tasks for moving, placing, and confirming delivery.
- **G32 -> AT6, AT7, AT8**: Sequential tasks for moving, parking, and confirming meal retrieval.
- **G4 -> AT9, AT10**: Parallel execution to gather patient info and check companionship simultaneously.
- **G7 -> G71, G72, G73**: OR decomposition as dishes can be retrieved by a single robot, human call, or two robots.
- **G8 -> G81, G82, G83**: OR decomposition for door opening by a single robot, human, or two robots.

This model ensures efficient and flexible execution of the delivery and retrieval process, considering various scenarios and cooperation possibilities.
